4.3 Fit to the Problem (C3) 

4.3.1 How the Technology Addresses the Problem

A Rule-Based Expert System is a suitable approach for the proposed UAPS ePelekat Kenderaan enhancement because the technology can evaluate application information and supporting documents based on predefined conditions rules. The existing application process requires users to provide several types of information and supporting documents to be processed without a clear validation guide that may cause a missing and invalid application information.

By implementing predefined IF-THEN rules, the proposed system can identify the missing information and invalid documents during the application process. The system will send a notification message to inform the user to take necessary actions for the submission before proceed to the next process. Therefore, integrating the rule-based validation features into a multi-step application form helps users to complete their application process without delay or errors.  

4.3.2 Benefits of Using Rule-Based Expert System 

1. Consistent Validation Results

A Rule-Based Expert System provides predefined conditions where it works to evaluate the information which allows the proposed enhancement system to provide consistent validation results when the same conditions are applied together. 

2. Clear Decision Making 

IF-THEN rules make the decision-making process more easier to understand since each condition will be connected to its specific actions. 

3. Reduced Incomplete Application Submission 

The predefined rules allow the system to identify missing information and invalid uploaded documents before the user can proceed to the next step which will help the users to complete their application form systematically. 

4.3.3 Limitations and Risks of Rule-Based Expert System 

1. Depending on the Predefined Rules 

The technology can only evaluate conditions that have been defined, additional conditions or document requirements are not included which make the system may not identify the issues. 

2. Require Accurate and Updated Knowledge 

The validation accuracy of the rules are stored in the knowledge base. Incorrect or outdated rules may produce wrong validation messages and prevent users from proceeding to the next step. 

3. Limited Flexibility to Handle Unexpected Situations

A Rule-Based system only follows predefined rules conditions and may not handle unexpected situations that are not covered by the rules statements. 

